# direnv: the flake's default shell in every shell that enters this folder (flake.nix; docs/development.md, "The Nix shells"): Python 3.14 with the tools' packages
# (.venv/default, .github/requirements/tools.txt), the Rust that dm/host/rust/rust-toolchain.toml names, .NET 10, zstd and SPIRV-Tools, Xcode's clang and make first.
# Run `direnv allow` once after reading this file. nix-direnv caches the shell; plain direnv evaluates the flake on each entry.
# The flake reads these files besides flake.nix and flake.lock, so a change to one of them reloads the shell too
watch_file dm/nix/shell_hook.sh dm/host/rust/rust-toolchain.toml .github/requirements/tools.txt
use flake
# This checkout's own additions (another shell, variables such as DM_GAME), not committed
source_env_if_exists .envrc.local
